+| R3 | **Restore** writes into a new directory only, never over a drive; a failure leaves nothing. Every parent must be a directory the restore created; files are created with `O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW`; only regular files, directories, symlinks, and 0/0 whiteouts are allowed (V17). Owners, setuid and setgid bits, the opaque marker, whiteouts and absolute symlinks are restored only beneath the machine layers (`Layout.Layers`), owners only as root (`KeepOwners`), and never setuid on a uid-0 file or setgid to gid 0. Elsewhere a symlink must stay inside its own root. The vault root gets the vault's user, 0600 files and 0700 directories; top-level roots are 0700; the vault and key-slot file must be regular files. The owner session's unlock ends. **Restoring from the old drive** is the same path (a backup piped into a restore) without the MAC: nothing authenticates a drive's plaintext broker state, so the restore is marked `Unverified` and its owner number and grants count as the owner's only after the tier-4 re-confirmation. Outside the machine layers a symlink must be relative with no `..` element, stay in its root, not target a machine layer or a directory above one, and no accepted link's target may run through another accepted link in either restore order, so a chain like `a -> .`, `b -> a/..` cannot reach outside (security review 2, finding 2; SR2-2; L3 on #151). Layer links are guest-relative: they resolve inside the guest's root and are never the end of a host-side resolution, so no host-side link may lead into or above a layer. The box's own state outside the layers makes no such links. | REC-1, V17 | — |
